meta {
  name: Set summon bounty
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/summons/bonus
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "username": "{{playerUser}}",
    "multiplierPct": 100,
    "note": "set by the Bruno collection"
  }
}

tests {
  test("saves the multiplier", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.getBody().bonuses).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  Puts a multiplier on an account: summoning any of **its** characters pays the
  summoner `multiplierPct`% of the usual points. 200 is double, 0 makes
  summoning that account worth nothing, and the ceiling is 1000 (10×).

  The multiplier is on the *summoned* account — it does nothing for that
  account's own summons.

  Sent as `100` here (the normal rate) so running the collection cannot quietly
  leave a bounty on the realm — it does leave a visible `1×` row in the panel
  that you can Remove. Delete one with
  `DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/summons/bonus?accountId=<id>`; the current list
  comes back on the response of either call, and also from
  `Admin / Get summon rewards`.
}
